          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            (map) is
            %em differentiable
            at some point if it can be well approximated by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            near that point. The approximating linear maps at different points together form the
            %em derivative
            of the map.
          %p
            One may then ask whether the derivative itself is differentiable, and so on. This leads to a hierarchy of ever more differentiable maps, starting with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
            and progressing through maps that are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            times (continuously) differentiable to those that are infinitely differentiable, and finally to those that are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+map"} analytic
            = succeed "." do
              %em smooth
          %p
            Differentiability is first defined directly for maps between (open subsets of) a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifold
            %em between
            differentiable manifolds, forming a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            less differentiable manifold, we may always consider maps that are less differentiable than the manifolds between which they run.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            In all of the following
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
