                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is twice differentiable, for then we can write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi w
                          %mo +
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo +
                              %mi v
                              %mo +
                              %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi d
                          %mi f
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi w
                          %mo ,
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi v
                            %mo +
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo +
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  f(x+v+w+h) &amp;= f(x+v+w) + d f_{x+v+w}(h) + E {|h|}\\
                  \&amp;= f(x+v+w) + d f_x(h) + d(d f)_x(v+w,h) + E {|v+w|}{|h|} + E{|h|}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo +
                  %mi w
                  %mo ,
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(d f)_x(v+w,h)
            can also be incorporated into the error term. Of course, setting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h=0
            we obtain the characterization of twice-differentiability from the previous section. But setting
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mi w
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v=w=0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is differentiable at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            with derivative
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f_x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p
            Secondly, the virtue of a second differential incorporating the first derivatives is that like the first differential
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mn 2
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^2 f
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy%27s+invariant+rule"} Cauchy's invariant rule
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+rule"} chain rule
            for second differentials of composite maps simply by substitution: if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = f(u)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = g(x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2 y
            in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d u
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2 u
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d u
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2 u
            in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2 x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2 y
            in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d x
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2 x
          %p In fact, this can be proven using the above direct characterization of the second differential, in essentially exactly the same way that we prove the ordinary chain rule for first derivatives. We sketch the proof, omitting the explicit error terms. We can write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi v
                  %mo +
                  %mi w
                  %mo +
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(f(x+v+w+h)) - g(f(x+v)) - g(f(x+w)) + g(f(x))
          %p as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mi w
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mi h
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi w
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(f(x) + v' + w' + h') - g(f(x) + v') - g(f(x) + w') + g(f(x))
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' = f(x+v) - f(x)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' = f(x+w) - f(x)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi v
                    %mo +
                    %mi w
                    %mo +
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h' = f(x+v+w+h) - f(x+v) - f(x+w) + f(x)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∂
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^2 g_{f(x)}(v',w') + d g_{f(x)}(h').
          %p
            But by differentiability of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ≈
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' \approx d f_x(v)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ≈
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' \approx d f_x(w)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ≈
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h' \approx \partial^2 f_x(v,w) + d f_x(h)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∂
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∂
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^2 g_{f(x)}(d f_x(v), d f_x(w)) + d g_{f(x)}(\partial^2 f_x(v,w) + d f_x(h))
          %p which is exactly what we would get by substitution.
          %h3#for_maps_between_manifolds For maps between manifolds
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^k
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifolds"} differentiable manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            times differentiable, or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\le k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are smooth (infinitely differentiable) manifolds, so that we can define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^n
            functions between them for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\le \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            A differentiable map between manifolds induces a map between their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundles"} tangent bundles
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f : T X \to T Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{k+1}
            manifolds and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{k+1}
            maps to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^k
            manifolds and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^k
            maps. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
            for more.
          %h2#examples_and_nonexamples Examples and non-examples
          %h3#DifferentiabilityOpposedToPartialDifferentiability Differentiability versus partial differentiability
          %p
            The function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi y
                                  %mn 3
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo +
                                %msup
                                  %mi y
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ≠
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f(x,y) =
                  \\begin{cases}
                  \\frac{y^3}{x^2+y^2} &amp;\quad (x,y) \neq (0,0)\\
                  0 &amp;\quad (x,y) = (0,0)
                  \\end{cases}
          %p
            is continuous everywhere, and has directional derivatives (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectionalDerivative"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
            in all directions, but is not differentiable at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
            in the sense of def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DerivativeOfFunctionFromRnToR"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi b
                          %mn 3
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi b
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{b^3}{a^2+b^2}
          %p
            One may wonder whether existence of a linear map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f_x
            is enough, but this is also not the case. The function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi y
                                  %mn 3
                              %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                            %mi x
                            %mo ≠
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                            %mi x
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x,y) = \begin{cases} \frac{y^3}{x} &amp;\quad x\neq 0\\ 0 &amp;\quad x=0 \end{cases}
          %p
            has all directional derivatives at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
            equaling
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f_{(0,0)}
            whose values are the directional derivatives. But it is not differentiable at
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
          %p
            The discontinuity kind of gives this last one away; maybe a continuous function with linear directional derivatives must be differentiable? But no, because if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is a
            %span.newWikiWord
              Weierstrass function
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Weierstrass+function"} ?
            (continuous everywhere but differentiable nowhere) from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+function"} period
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\pi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} atan2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{atan2}
            is a
            = succeed "-argument" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arctangent"} arctangent
            function from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            (so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi sin
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} atan2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{x^2+y^2} \,\sin\,\operatorname{atan2}(y,x) = y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi cos
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} atan2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{x^2+y^2} \,\cos\,\operatorname{atan2}(y,x) = x
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} atan2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x,y) = (x^2 + y^2) W(\operatorname{atan2}(y,x)) .
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is, like
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/1497043/is-there-a-function-thats-continuous-and-has-all-directional-derivatives-as-a-l"} Math StackExchange question 1497043
          %h3#differentiability_versus_continuous_and_higher_differentiability Differentiability versus continuous and higher differentiability
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi k
                  %mi sin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_k(x) \coloneqq x^k \sin(1/x)
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            to itself, with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(0) \coloneqq 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_k
            is smooth (even analytic); but at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0
            is not continuous,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1
            is continuous but not differentiable,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_2
            is differentiable but not continuously differentiable, and so on:
          %ul
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 2 n
              is even, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_k
              is differentiable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              times but not continuously differentiable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              times;
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 2 n + 1
              is odd, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_k
              is continuously differentiable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              times but not differentiable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n + 1
              times.
          %p
            (For a fractional value of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_k
            has the same behaviour as
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⌈
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⌉
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{\lceil{k}\rceil}
          %p Similarly, in two dimensions we can consider functions such as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi sin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi y
                          %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x,y) = (x^2+y^2)\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}).
          %p
            together with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
