          %p
            Uniform differentiability is stronger than continuous differentiability but independent of twice differentiability. For an example that is uniformly differentiable but not twice differentiable, use
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_3
            again. For an example that that is twice differentiable (and hence continuously differentiable) but not uniformly differentiable, use
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
